WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.940
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs

01:35.030 --> 01:39.990
Episode 4:
A Great Gift

02:07.860 --> 02:08.630
Hey!

02:16.120 --> 02:17.510
What's this?

02:20.330 --> 02:22.940
Mr. Vitalis, what is this?

02:23.930 --> 02:25.930
It's violin sheet music.

02:25.950 --> 02:28.940
It contains musical notes for playing the violin.

02:28.950 --> 02:29.900
Musical notes?

02:30.300 --> 02:33.140
With them you can play music.

02:34.660 --> 02:37.860
This is a violin concerto by Tchaikovsky.

02:39.730 --> 02:40.830
Is that what it says?

02:41.300 --> 02:43.870
You... can't read?

02:44.120 --> 02:44.980
No, I don't know how.

02:45.400 --> 02:46.450
Didn't you attend school?

02:47.180 --> 02:49.410
There was no school in my village.

02:52.010 --> 02:58.420
To be a part of the Vitalis Troupe you must know how to read.

02:58.710 --> 03:04.700
But don't you need a mayor or a priest to learn how to read and write?

03:05.630 --> 03:09.290
Capi can teach you later.
- Capi reads?

03:14.800 --> 03:18.520
Now for the next act, some riddles.

03:18.740 --> 03:25.670
What animal has big ears, claws, and is referred to as a "she"?

03:43.650 --> 03:45.610
They got it, a cat.

03:49.630 --> 03:54.250
Now, if you'd please make one last trip.

03:54.410 --> 03:57.120
In the end, what do people want to be?

04:08.560 --> 04:12.130
A king? I see.

04:12.480 --> 04:14.160
That's true, isn't it?

04:20.000 --> 04:24.630
Please offer these intelligent animals a little reward.

04:29.300 --> 04:31.310
All right, I can do this.

04:31.460 --> 04:35.890
If Capi and Dolce can read and write, I won't be left out. I'll do my best.

04:45.850 --> 04:49.420
Now, we'll start with the alphabet first.

04:50.350 --> 05:05.690
A, B, C, D, E, F, G...
- A, B, C, D, E, F, G...

05:08.290 --> 05:12.920
Y, Z.
-Y, Z.

05:13.910 --> 05:17.990
Hey, how do you write my name?
- Your name?

05:22.270 --> 05:25.000
Remy. This is how you write Remy.

05:27.560 --> 05:30.930
Hey, how do you write Capi?
- Capi?

05:31.350 --> 05:33.840
Capi's name is like this.

05:33.970 --> 05:36.020
Wow! And Dolce?

05:37.250 --> 05:38.690
Dolce's is...

05:42.850 --> 05:49.710
R-I-V-I-E-R-E. That's river.

05:55.310 --> 05:59.360
And... How do you spell tree?

06:00.290 --> 06:05.230
A-R-B-R-E. That's it!

06:06.480 --> 06:11.510
Flower is F-L-E-U-R.

06:23.260 --> 06:28.680
Star is E-T-O-I-L-E.

06:29.100 --> 06:33.200
Moon is L-U-N-E.

06:50.480 --> 06:52.790
This city is so big.

06:53.700 --> 06:58.150
It's very busy here.
We should be able to stay for two weeks.

06:58.410 --> 07:05.290
Oh! That sign! Wine is sold there.
Isn't that right? Is that what it says?

07:07.450 --> 07:09.430
Madeleine's Pharmacy.

07:10.890 --> 07:12.690
Men's Tailoring.

07:13.510 --> 07:14.830
Pastries.

07:15.410 --> 07:19.620
It's amazing how I used to not be able to read anything.

07:19.920 --> 07:22.460
One day you will be able to read a book.

07:22.720 --> 07:26.120
They use them at church, right? I've seen that before.

07:26.670 --> 07:31.450
That's the Bible. But there are many others to read.

07:31.720 --> 07:32.860
Others?

07:39.520 --> 07:42.910
This is a book about India.
- India?

07:44.080 --> 07:47.300
Even if you've been living in France, Remy, and haven't been to India,

07:47.610 --> 07:51.580
by reading this book it'd be as if you were there.

07:52.810 --> 07:55.460
As if I was there?
- Yes.

07:56.580 --> 07:58.320
This is a history book.

08:00.170 --> 08:02.990
Who's this person?
- Cleopatra.

08:03.920 --> 08:07.910
By reading this book, you will learn about the history of an Egyptian queen.

08:08.310 --> 08:10.710
She lived thousands of years ago.

08:12.210 --> 08:13.950
These books are really amazing.

08:14.720 --> 08:20.010
By reading books, you can learn a lot of things you do not know.

08:20.410 --> 08:22.720
There are many things I don't know.

08:23.930 --> 08:29.030
But, do you even have enough leisure time to read them?

08:29.310 --> 08:32.220
We have a lot of time to study and learn.

08:32.990 --> 08:37.330
Don't judge by appearances. We should always strive to enrich our knowledge.

08:42.050 --> 08:42.850
Hey.

08:43.150 --> 08:45.750
Well, well... Mr. Coral!

08:46.900 --> 08:48.710
I'm sorry to bother you.

08:48.930 --> 08:55.100
A first class writer like Mr. Coral would never bother us.

08:55.670 --> 08:57.370
That man's famous?

08:57.590 --> 09:01.560
Coral's a well-known novelist.

09:02.040 --> 09:07.560
So, how's my book selling?
- It's a big success.

09:07.970 --> 09:12.570
Especially "Ten Magical Tales".
Even I have read them.

09:12.830 --> 09:14.530
They're really great.

09:13.740 --> 09:16.160
"Ten Magical Tales".

09:14.560 --> 09:19.170
Mr. Coral, I really, really admire you.

09:19.650 --> 09:23.140
I don't think there's any comparable writer in France.

09:23.360 --> 09:27.390
It's also been well received in Paris.
- What's that book about?

09:30.300 --> 09:32.790
She's just a traveling artist.

09:33.100 --> 09:36.210
I'm Remy of the Vitalis Troupe.

09:36.560 --> 09:40.950
Oh, are you interested in my book?

09:41.370 --> 09:42.090
Yes.

09:46.190 --> 09:50.290
Look, in the magic kingdom there's a tree that grows books.

09:50.400 --> 09:56.380
A tree that grows books?
- In my book, there's a story about this tree.

09:58.250 --> 10:00.610
Sounds great!

10:01.120 --> 10:02.330
The usual.

10:02.590 --> 10:06.160
Yes, yes, your paper and envelopes.

10:12.290 --> 10:15.020
One day, you'll be able to read my book.

10:16.300 --> 10:19.010
Me? I can really read your book?

10:20.400 --> 10:21.370
Of course.

10:21.920 --> 10:24.370
Goodbye, Mr. Coral!

10:31.220 --> 10:32.500
You want to read it?

10:33.230 --> 10:33.890
Yes.

10:34.570 --> 10:39.000
You can have the book but you'll have to pay five francs.

10:39.620 --> 10:42.840
Five francs? This book is very expensive.

10:43.190 --> 10:44.960
Move on please.

10:45.340 --> 10:46.920
You're wasting my time.

10:47.910 --> 10:49.320
Remy, let's go.

10:56.790 --> 10:59.830
"Ten Magical Tales".

11:01.550 --> 11:03.100
I really want to read them.

11:18.150 --> 11:21.390
It's hopeless, the book is too expensive.

11:22.070 --> 11:25.510
It's impossible for me to read books.

11:30.210 --> 11:31.530
What is it, Joli-Coeur?

11:42.970 --> 11:44.760
Huh, what's that?

11:48.970 --> 11:52.320
"Ten Magical Tales".

11:58.400 --> 12:06.030
The first story is the tale of the princess and the balloon.

12:07.660 --> 12:10.760
A long, long time ago, in a far away land...

12:26.520 --> 12:31.860
The magician turned the princess's brother into a snail.

12:32.480 --> 12:34.660
So what did the princess do?

12:37.460 --> 12:41.160
To save her brother, she went on a journey in a balloon.

12:41.380 --> 12:43.540
I heard it at least ten times yesterday.

12:45.110 --> 12:49.380
This letter must be a gift from Mr. Coral.

12:49.930 --> 12:54.650
Because the envelopes Mr. Coral bought were the same.

12:55.180 --> 12:56.190
Well...

12:56.540 --> 12:59.410
Zerbino, come, time for your stunt training.

13:03.470 --> 13:05.010
What's wrong, Joli-Coeur?

13:10.920 --> 13:12.940
It's here! Another letter!

13:14.330 --> 13:17.950
The second story from "Ten Magical Tales".

13:19.310 --> 13:21.940
The story of the giant lurking in the desert.

13:27.870 --> 13:32.300
The third story from "Ten Magical Tales".

13:33.910 --> 13:38.520
A long time ago, there was a traveling merchant who sold happiness.

13:38.710 --> 13:43.500
The message "I will sell you happiness" was printed in gold on the outside of his big bag.

13:43.520 --> 13:47.750
Only unhappy people could see the message.

13:49.510 --> 13:54.290
Many people in the land bought happiness from him.

13:54.890 --> 14:01.770
The merchant took a lot of things from his bag for the people to see.

14:05.910 --> 14:07.740
Yes, yes, well done.

14:08.420 --> 14:10.030
That's the way to do it, Zerbino.

14:11.220 --> 14:13.250
All right, once more.

14:14.510 --> 14:19.360
The ninth story is about a dragon trapped in a castle of ice.

14:20.020 --> 14:23.430
A long time ago in a distant land, there was an evil dragon.

14:24.140 --> 14:27.670
He turned people into stone and sank the city to the bottom of the sea.

14:27.910 --> 14:35.730
Finally the dragon aroused the wrath of God and he was locked up in the ice castle.

14:38.160 --> 14:43.600
For over 300 hundred years, no one came to the castle.

14:43.910 --> 14:49.750
Alone, the dragon's grudge continued.
Why did this happen to him?

14:50.240 --> 14:54.250
After 1001 years had passed like this...

14:58.260 --> 15:02.200
Anyone here? I've lost my way.

15:11.640 --> 15:17.790
You're now trapped here.
You cannot leave this place.

15:18.690 --> 15:20.390
The princess was very surprised.

15:20.790 --> 15:24.890
But she felt more sadness than fear overflow in her heart.

15:25.830 --> 15:29.140
Why are you crying?

15:30.460 --> 15:35.440
Poor dragon, you've been alone for more than a thousand years.

15:36.610 --> 15:44.260
The dragon was surprised, she was actually crying for him. He had never seen such tears.

15:45.540 --> 15:50.710
From that day on, the princess stayed with the dragon to play the harp for him.

15:51.400 --> 15:59.330
Thanks to the princess the dragon felt peaceful, for the first time in his life.

16:00.900 --> 16:04.520
But the princess's sadness was not consoled.

16:05.330 --> 16:11.030
God, please forgive the dragon. The dragon has already been punished enough.

16:11.170 --> 16:15.040
The dragon committed a great sin by letting people suffer.

16:15.380 --> 16:20.040
The life of someone who truly loves him must be exchanged,

16:20.390 --> 16:21.890
in order for him to be forgiven.

16:21.910 --> 16:23.800
Please, take my life.

16:37.120 --> 16:41.940
Dragon, my spirit will always be by your side.

16:44.680 --> 16:46.510
What are you doing!?

16:59.490 --> 17:08.000
The dragon was free. His tears turned into beautiful stars that fell to the earth.

17:10.600 --> 17:15.520
Since then, no one has ever seen a dragon.

17:20.670 --> 17:25.560
"My spirit will always be by your side."

17:29.020 --> 17:29.640
Remy.

17:30.850 --> 17:32.840
Why haven't you done what I asked?

17:33.300 --> 17:36.120
Ah! No, I haven't. I'm sorry!

17:39.270 --> 17:40.750
Well, let's continue.

17:52.480 --> 17:54.990
Thank you very much.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.200
Mr. Coral!

17:56.380 --> 17:58.780
Congratulations, Mr. Coral.

17:59.380 --> 18:03.500
You've finally obtained the literary award.
- Wonderful!

18:03.870 --> 18:08.040
Because of that you're now known as a leading writer. Congratulations.

18:08.610 --> 18:09.250
Thank you.

18:09.650 --> 18:12.200
Excuse me. Excuse me.

18:14.560 --> 18:18.400
Mr. Coral, thank you very much.

18:20.230 --> 18:23.470
I'm Remy.
- Remy?

18:23.910 --> 18:28.710
I met you at the bookstore.
- Oh, that's right.

18:28.870 --> 18:32.130
I must thank you for the letters.

18:32.130 --> 18:34.840
Letters? What are you talking about?

18:36.120 --> 18:38.350
Umm...
- Hey!

18:38.570 --> 18:44.140
You can't just wander in here.
I'm sorry, I'll escort her out now.

18:44.430 --> 18:49.560
Ah, please do. I have no idea what this girl is talking about.

18:49.670 --> 18:52.210
Well, come on!

19:09.450 --> 19:10.750
Oh, the girl from before.

19:11.670 --> 19:14.330
Does your master have any more sheet music?

19:14.350 --> 19:18.360
I'd be willing to buy them.

19:19.140 --> 19:22.100
Sheet music?
- You don't know?

19:23.440 --> 19:29.330
Let me see the sheet music, please.
- But it's closing time.

19:29.860 --> 19:31.050
Here, this is it.

19:32.020 --> 19:33.450
It was about ten days ago.

19:34.200 --> 19:37.920
Your master asked me to buy this.

19:40.570 --> 19:44.890
Ah, he was seventeen years old when he bought this.

19:45.110 --> 19:48.990
It's been kept in very good condition.

19:51.080 --> 19:55.180
Why!? Why would he want to sell such an important thing?

19:55.230 --> 20:00.870
Well, he used the money to buy envelopes, paper and ink.

20:07.310 --> 20:13.940
The first story of "Ten Magical Tales" is the tale of the timid crow.

20:20.510 --> 20:21.150
No!

20:21.350 --> 20:25.370
Those letters weren't really Mr. Coral's stories.
They were...

20:51.210 --> 20:52.730
Mr. Vitalis!

20:57.190 --> 21:01.910
Your sheet music...
You sold your treasures.

21:03.730 --> 21:05.410
All for my sake.

21:09.110 --> 21:09.960
Thank you.

21:10.900 --> 21:14.050
They were the greatest gifts ever.
Thank you!

21:14.400 --> 21:22.250
Surely, living is wonderful

21:18.480 --> 21:22.160
Remy, the stories aren't finished yet.

21:24.140 --> 21:35.080
My hand is upon the left side of my beating chest...

21:24.220 --> 21:25.360
Will you listen?

21:28.070 --> 21:31.810
The tenth story of "Ten Magical Tales".

21:32.630 --> 21:38.320
A long time ago, in a far away land,

21:35.380 --> 21:45.150
Tomorrow start walking

21:39.290 --> 21:44.500
there was a beautiful lake where many animals lived harmoniously.

21:44.580 --> 21:45.440
One day...

21:45.260 --> 21:55.160
You won't cross paths with happiness

21:55.280 --> 22:03.290
Try to look at them more

22:04.900 --> 22:08.560
You're beautiful now that

22:08.780 --> 22:20.640
Your eyes are filled with laughter

22:20.990 --> 22:30.750
Tomorrow promises that

22:30.910 --> 22:40.690
There will always be mistakes but

22:40.960 --> 22:49.800
Try to seek for them more

22:50.570 --> 22:54.180
Give your heart to

22:54.470 --> 23:07.500
That person who is also seeking you

23:19.410 --> 23:20.710
Why are you crying?

23:24.340 --> 23:27.840
Nina is unable to speak.

23:30.020 --> 23:32.880
Mr. Vitalis, looks like a big audience.

23:32.900 --> 23:36.770
<i>Miracle of the St. Maria Statue</i>

23:32.900 --> 23:36.770
Next time:
